kh-ramabs: a point32le layout, for guests that keep the pointer as two int32

BeOS R5's app_server keeps its pointer coordinate as two little-endian
int32, where Rhapsody DR2 keeps a Point{int16 x, int16 y} and classic Mac
OS keeps a big-endian Point with VERTICAL first.  Width is the third
independent axis of the layout table 0009 introduced, so this is one branch
in each of the two offset-taking accessors plus the realize-time string
parse -- the accessors are the only two places that know a wire format.

The point buffer widens from 4 to 8 bytes and the transfer length becomes
kh_pt_bytes() rather than sizeof(b), so a 4-byte layout still reads and
writes exactly 4 bytes and the Mac profile's multi-offset writes are
unaffected.

No VMStateDescription is added, so `-device kh-ramabs` still leaves a
station's device set and its golden checkpoint untouched.

Derived and proven on beos: see docs/lab/BEOS-ABSOLUTE-POINTER.md.

